len. <year>1998</year>. The <italic>Drosophila</italic> sanpodo gene controls sibling cell fate and encodes a tropomodulin homolog, an actin/tropomyosin-associated protein. <source>Development.</source> <volume>125</volume>:<fpage>1845</fpage>&#x02013;1856.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9550717</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Fowler, V.M. <year>1996</year>. Regulation of actin filament length in erythrocytes and striated muscle. <source>Curr. Opin. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>8</volume>:<fpage>86</fpage>&#x02013;96.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8791408</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Fowler, V.M. <year>1997</year>. Capping actin filament growth: tropomodulin in muscle and nonmuscle cells. <source>Soc. Gen. Physiol. Ser.</source> <volume>52</volume>:<fpage>79</fpage>&#x02013;89.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9210222</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Fowler, V.M., M.A. Sussmann, P.G. Miller, B.E. Flucher, and M.P. Daniels. <year>1993</year>. Tropomodulin is associated with the free (pointed) ends of the thin filaments in rat skeletal muscle. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>120</volume>:<fpage>411</fpage>&#x02013;420.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8421055</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Gregorio, C.C., and P.B. Antin. <year>2000</year>. To the heart of myofibril assembly. <source>Trends Cell Biol.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>355</fpage>&#x02013;362.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10932092</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Gregorio, C.C., A. Weber, M. Bondad, C.R. Pennise, and V.M. Fowler. <year>1995</year>. Requirement of pointed-end capping by tropomodulin to maintain actin filament length in embryonic chick cardiac myocytes. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>377</volume>:<fpage>83</fpage>&#x02013;86.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7544875</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id