 S.A. Witt, and T.R. Kimball. <year>1998</year>b. Myofibril degeneration caused by tropomodulin overexpression leads to dilated cardiomyopathy in juvenile mice. <source>J. Clin. Invest.</source> <volume>101</volume>:<fpage>51</fpage>&#x02013;61.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9421465</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib36"><citation citation-type="journal">van Straaten, M., D. Goulding, B. Kolmerer, S. Labeit, J. Clayton, K. Leonard, and B. Bullard. <year>1999</year>. Association of kettin with actin in the Z-disc of insect flight muscle. <source>J. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>285</volume>:<fpage>1549</fpage>&#x02013;1562.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9917396</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="fn1"><label>*</label><p>Abbreviations used in this paper: APF, after pupal formation&#x0003b; D<sub>H</sub>, H zone&#x0003b; D<sub>Z</sub>, Z-disc&#x0003b; IFM, indirect flight muscle&#x0003b; SPDO, sanpodo&#x0003b; TM, tropomyosin&#x0003b; Tmod, tropomodulin&#x0003b; TOT, Tmod-overexpressing transgenic.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>